cause: MAINTENANCE
effect: DETOUR
header_text {
  translation {
    text: "Shuttle buses replacing A Line westbound from 5:25 AM to 1:12 PM on Sun Jun 28 due to maintenance."
    language: "en"
  }
}
description_text {
  translation {
    text: "Shuttle buses replacing A Line eastbound from 5:25 AM to 1:12 PM on Sun Jun 28 due to maintenance.\r\n\nRTD will conduct essential maintenance on the A Line on Sunday, June 28, between approximately 5:25 a.m. and 1:12 p.m. During this period, commuter rail service will be suspended between Denver Airport and 61st-Pena stations. Customers are advised to plan accordingly and allow additional travel time to connect to and from the airport.\r\n\nRegular A Line service will continue to operate between Denver Union Station and 61st-Pena Station.\r\n\nThe scheduled work will improve the commuter rail line’s overall reliability and safety. Bus shuttles will support A Line service between the two impacted stations and will not mirror regular train schedules.\r\n\nBus shuttle boarding locations are as follows:\r\n\n    Denver Airport Station: Arrivals at Gate 6; Departures at Gate 7\r\n\nLocated at the DEN Transit Center, Level 1, adjacent to the Westin Denver International Airport Hotel. The DEN Transit Center can be accessed at the south end of Jeppesen Terminal by exiting through the glass doors and taking the escalator or elevator down to ground level.\r\n\n    61st-Pena Station: In front of the station\r\n\nRail service to the airport will resume following completion of the work. The first train with continuous service to the Denver Airport Station is scheduled to depart Union Station at approximately 12:30 p.m. The first train with continuous service to Union Station is expected to depart Denver Airport Station at approximately 1:27 p.m.\r\n\nAffected stops:\r\nDenver Airport Station (#34476)"
    language: "en"
  }
}
